    "attrs": {
      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\r\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\r\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"2\">Level 2 - Beginner</span>\r\n    <span class=\"time\">35 min</span>\r\n    <span class=\"chip\">Pattern primer</span>\r\n    <span class=\"chip\">Intervals</span>\r\n  </div>\r\n  <h1>Intervals</h1>\r\n  <p class=\"lead\">Almost every interval problem is \"sort, then walk once\". The only real choices are what you sort by (start or end) and what you carry during the walk: the last merged block, a heap of end times, or a running counter. This page builds the seven templates you need: merge, insert, intersect, can-attend, maximum non-overlapping, minimum rooms, and the difference array or sweep line.</p>\r\n  <p class=\"small prereq\"><b>Go deeper:</b> <a href=\"{{BASE}}coding/coding-range-query\">Range queries: Fenwick tree, segment tree, ordered map</a>.</p>\r\n"
  },
